---
components: ["TransferList"]
description: A dual list box that moves items between an available list and a selected list, with search, reordering, drag and drop, and form support.
---

<script>
  import { Stack, TransferList } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  const items = [
    { id: "billing", text: "Billing administrator" },
    { id: "audit", text: "Audit log viewer" },
    { id: "deploy", text: "Deploy to production" },
    { id: "keys", text: "Manage API keys" },
    { id: "members", text: "Invite members" },
    { id: "alerts", text: "Edit alert rules" },
    { id: "sso", text: "Configure single sign-on", disabled: true },
    { id: "support", text: "Open support cases" },
  ];
</script>

## Basic

Pass the choices as `items` and bind `selectedIds`, the ids the selected list
holds in the order it shows them. The available list holds the rest, in the
order of `items`.

Click a row to mark it, hold <DocKbd label="Shift" /> to mark a range, then
press an add or remove button, double-click a row, or press <DocKbd label="Enter" />
to move the marked rows. With no row marked, <DocKbd label="Enter" /> moves the row under the cursor.

<FileSource src="/framed/TransferList/TransferListBasic" />

## Usage

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Use a transfer list to build a set from a long list of choices, or when the order of the set matters. | Two lists show both what is chosen and what is left, which a multi-select menu hides. |
| Use a [MultiSelect](/components/MultiSelect) or [CheckboxGroup](/components/CheckboxGroup) for a short list where order does not matter. | Moving rows between lists takes more steps than checking a box. |
| Set `legendText` to name the whole field, such as "Workspace permissions". | The two lists sit in a group with that name, so a screen reader announces it with each list. |
| Turn on `filterable` once a list passes about ten items. | Searching each list is faster than scrolling, and a long list is windowed so searching stays quick. |
| Keep `reorderable` on when the order is a priority, and off when it is not. | The selected list is submitted in order, so a user who cannot see that order matters will not set it. |

## Keyboard

Each list is a multi-select listbox with one tab stop, and the cursor moves
with the arrow keys while focus stays on the list. The move buttons are a
toolbar with one tab stop, and every arrow key moves between its buttons.

| Key | Action |
| --- | --- |
| <DocKbd label="Up" /> / <DocKbd label="Down" /> | Move the cursor. |
| <DocKbd label="Shift" />+<DocKbd label="Up" /> / <DocKbd label="Down" /> | Mark the rows from where the range started. |
| <DocKbd label="Space" /> | Mark or unmark the row under the cursor. <DocKbd label="Shift" />+<DocKbd label="Space" /> marks a range. |
| <DocKbd label="Ctrl" />+<DocKbd label="A" /> | Mark every row. <DocKbd label="Escape" /> clears the marks. |
| <DocKbd label="Enter" /> | Move the marked rows to the other list. |
| <DocKbd label="Delete" /> / <DocKbd label="Backspace" /> | In the selected list, move the marked rows back. |
| <DocKbd label="Alt" />+<DocKbd label="Up" /> / <DocKbd label="Down" /> | In the selected list, move the marked rows up or down. |
| Printable characters | Move the cursor to the next row that starts with them. |

Moves are announced to screen readers, such as "Audit log viewer moved to
position 2 of 3."

## Filterable

Set `filterable` to add a search field to each list. A search narrows what a
list shows, and the buttons that move all items move the rows left by the
search. Marks on rows the search hides are dropped. Set `shouldFilterItem` to
match on more than the item's text.

<FileSource src="/framed/TransferList/TransferListFilterable" />

## Reordering

The selected list can be reordered with the up and down buttons above it, with
<DocKbd label="Alt" />+<DocKbd label="Up" /> and <DocKbd label="Down" />, or by dragging a row. Set `reorderable` to `false` to keep the
list in the order rows were added.

<TransferList
  {items}
  selectedIds={["deploy", "audit", "keys"]}
  reorderable={false}
  legendText="Fixed order"
/>

## Drag and drop

With a mouse or pen, drag a row, or all the marked rows, onto the other list.
Drop onto the selected list to choose where the rows land, and drop selected
rows onto the available list to remove them. Touch screens scroll instead, so
use the buttons there. Set `dragDrop` to `false` to turn dragging off.

<TransferList
  {items}
  selectedIds={["audit"]}
  dragDrop={false}
  legendText="Buttons and keys only"
/>

## Sizes

Set `size` to control row and button height. The default is `"md"`.

<Stack gap={7}>
  <TransferList {items} selectedIds={["audit"]} size="sm" rows={4} legendText="Small" />
  <TransferList {items} selectedIds={["audit"]} size="lg" rows={4} legendText="Large" />
</Stack>

## Layout

Set `rows` to control how many rows each list shows before it scrolls. The
default is 8. Below the medium breakpoint the lists stack, and the arrows on
the move buttons turn to point down and up. In right-to-left pages the lists
swap sides and the arrows mirror.

## States

Reflect validation and interaction states. A disabled item stays where it is,
and the buttons that move all items skip it.

### Invalid and warning

Set `invalid` and `invalidText`, or `warn` and `warnText`. Set `required` to
block a form from submitting with nothing selected.

<Stack gap={7}>
  <TransferList
    {items}
    selectedIds={[]}
    invalid
    invalidText="Select at least one permission."
    legendText="Invalid"
  />
  <TransferList
    {items}
    selectedIds={["billing", "deploy"]}
    warn
    warnText="Billing administrators can see every invoice."
    legendText="Warning"
  />
</Stack>

### Disabled and read-only

Set `disabled` to prevent interaction. Set `readonly` to let the lists scroll
and mark rows without moving them.

<Stack gap={7}>
  <TransferList {items} selectedIds={["audit"]} disabled legendText="Disabled" />
  <TransferList {items} selectedIds={["audit"]} readonly legendText="Read-only" />
</Stack>

## Large lists

Lists of a hundred items or more render only the rows in view, so 2,000 items
filter and move in a frame or two. Moving a long list through a form submits one
hidden input per selected item.

<FileSource src="/framed/TransferList/TransferListLarge" />

## Form

Set `name` to submit the selected ids, one entry per item, in the order the
selected list shows. `FormData.getAll(name)` returns them in order. A form reset
puts the selection back to what it was on first render.

<FileSource src="/framed/TransferList/TransferListForm" />

## Cancel a move

Each move dispatches `move` before the lists change. Its `detail` holds the
`ids` that would move, the list they come `from` and go `to`, and the
`selectedIds` the move would set. Call `preventDefault()` to keep the lists as
they are, for example to save the change first and set `selectedIds` when the
save succeeds. `change` follows each move that is not canceled.

```svelte
<TransferList
  {items}
  bind:selectedIds
  on:move={(event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    save(event.detail.selectedIds).then(() => {
      selectedIds = event.detail.selectedIds;
    });
  }}
/>
```

## Text

Every string is a prop, so the component can be translated. Visible text ends
in `Text`, and text that only a screen reader reads ends in `Description`. Set
`countText` and `announcementDescription` to build the item counts and the move
announcements from their numbers.

<TransferList
  {items}
  selectedIds={["audit"]}
  availableTitleText="Disponibles"
  selectedTitleText="Elegidos"
  addText="Agregar los elegidos"
  addAllText="Agregar todos"
  removeText="Quitar los elegidos"
  removeAllText="Quitar todos"
  moveUpText="Subir"
  moveDownText="Bajar"
  countText={({ marked, shown, total }) => marked > 0 ? `${marked} de ${shown} elegidos` : `${shown} de ${total}`}
  announcementDescription={({ type, count }) => `${count} movidos (${type}).`}
  legendText="Permisos"
/>
